    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Situated in a prominent and highly convenient position on The Square in the heart of Louisburgh, this characterful two-bedroom townhouse presents an exciting opportunity to acquire a distinctive property in one of Mayo’s most popular West Coast towns. With shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities virtually on the doorstep, the property is particularly well suited as a holiday home, investment property or conveniently located permanent residence.\r\nReflecting the age and traditional character of the building, the property is unusual in shape and features a quirky, individual layout, adding to its charm and distinguishing it from a more conventional townhouse.\r\nOn entering the property, a tiled entrance hall provides a welcoming introduction to the accommodation. An attractive feature of the hallway is a small internal window on the right-hand side as you enter, providing a glimpse through to the living area and adding further character to the property's unusual layout. The entrance hall leads directly into the kitchen/dining area, while a separate doorway from the hall provides access to the living room.\r\nThe kitchen/dining area benefits from large windows providing natural light, a tiled floor and fitted kitchen, providing a practical and comfortable space for everyday dining.\r\nThe living room has a warm and inviting atmosphere, featuring a timber floor and solid fuel stove, creating a cosy focal point and an ideal space in which to relax. From the living area, two steps lead up to a useful utility space positioned to the rear of the house. This area provides additional storage and is plumbed for a washing machine, offering valuable practical space away from the main living accommodation. \r\nUpstairs, the property provides two bedrooms, both with wooden flooring and offering comfortable accommodation for family or guests with views out to the Square in Louisburgh. A separate staircase leads to a fully tiled shower room.\r\nA further feature is the loft space, which has a wooden floor and Velux window. From here, there are lovely views towards Croagh Patrick, adding an attractive scenic dimension to this centrally located property while also providing useful additional space and storage. Adjacent is a W.C.\r\nIt should be noted that the property does not have any private outdoor space. However, a particularly useful addition is the traditional stone storage shed situated adjacent to the property. This provides valuable storage and is ideal for bicycles, surfboards, wetsuits, outdoor equipment, tools, luggage and other items associated with a holiday home or everyday living.\r\nThe property's central location, combined with Louisburgh's popularity as a gateway to the spectacular beaches, coastline, mountains and outdoor attractions of West Mayo, gives it considerable appeal as a holiday home or investment opportunity. Its location and flexible accommodation could also offer potential for holiday letting or longer-term rental, subject to any necessary permissions and regulations."
      },
